<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helmut Schmidt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–2015</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helmut Schmidt (1918–2015) was a German Social Democratic politician who was chancellor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> from 1974 to 1982. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>'s senator for the interior he won national fame for directing rescue work during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> flood of 1962. As chancellor he steered the country through economic crises and left-wing terrorism and backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>'s deployment of new missiles in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helmut-schmidt.jpg" alt="Helmut Schmidt" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Schafgans · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundeskanzler_Helmut_Schmidt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
